WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.230
You just crossed the line where space begins.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.050
How did humans first get here?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:17.050
Peruvian engineer Pedro Paulet claimed he tested a liquid-fuel engine in the 1890s.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.350
The first documented liquid-fuel rocket flight came in 1926: two and a half seconds, twelve and a half metres.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.420
A sounding rocket doesn't go into orbit. It climbs, coasts, and falls,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.320
giving experiments a few minutes of weightlessness and a look at the upper atmosphere.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:47.570
With the engine off, everything on board falls together, so it all floats.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.800
NASA has flown sounding rockets for science for decades.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.230
Yours just joined that tradition.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:14.170
<v Goicochea>Twelve metres in 1926. A hundred kilometres today. Paulet would want us to keep going.

